{
    "background_story": "Sofia had always been fascinated by the ocean's secrets. As a renowned marine biologist, she dedicated her career to studying the majestic creatures of the coral reefs. Her specialty was the Tridacnidae family, commonly known as giant clams. Sofia spent years researching these gentle giants, uncovering the mysteries of their habitats, behaviors, and importance in the marine ecosystem. Her groundbreaking work led to the discovery of a new species of giant clam, which was later named Tridacna sofiae in her honor. Sofia's tireless efforts also helped establish marine protected areas, ensuring the conservation of these incredible creatures and the delicate balance of the coral reefs. Her passion for Tridacnidae had a profound impact on the scientific community and inspired a new generation of marine biologists.",
